
# StudentManagementAPI

A CRUD REST API for managing students and their enrolled courses, built using the same layered architecture as the InventoryManagementAPI.

## What It Does

Manages students and courses in a SQL Server database. Each student can have multiple courses (one-to-many relationship). Exposes a full CRUD API with Swagger documentation and includes a unit test.

## Tech Stack

- ASP.NET Core Web API (.NET 8)
- Entity Framework Core 8.0 (Code-First)
- SQL Server (LocalDB)
- Swagger / OpenAPI
- xUnit (unit testing)
- Moq (mocking)

## Architecture

```
StudentManagementAPI/
├── Controllers/        # StudentController — REST endpoints
├── Data/               # ApplicationDbContext
├── Models/             # Student, Course
├── Repositories/       # IStudentRepository, StudentRepository
├── appsettings.json    # Connection string → StudentDB
└── Program.cs          # DI registration

StudentManagementAPI.Tests/
└── StudentControllerTests.cs   # Unit test: GetStudent returns 404 when not found
```

## API Endpoints

| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|--------|----------|-------------|
| GET | `/api/student` | Get all students (with courses) |
| GET | `/api/student/{id}` | Get student by ID |
| POST | `/api/student` | Add a new student |
| PUT | `/api/student/{id}` | Update student details |
| DELETE | `/api/student/{id}` | Delete a student |

## How to Run

**Prerequisites:** Visual Studio 2022, .NET 8 SDK, SQL Server LocalDB

1. Open the solution in Visual Studio 2022
2. Install NuGet packages via Package Manager Console:
   ```
   Install-Package Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.SqlServer -Version 8.0.0
   Install-Package Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Tools -Version 8.0.0
   Install-Package Swashbuckle.AspNetCore
   ```
3. Run migrations:
   ```
   Add-Migration InitialCreate
   Update-Database
   ```
4. Press **F5** — Swagger UI available at `https://localhost:{port}/swagger`

